<title>UK: StanChart sees positive Asia-Pacific.</title>
<headline>StanChart sees positive Asia-Pacific.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Chartered Plc, the London-based bank, said on Wednesday that it sees positive economic signs from its main Asia-Pacific region franchise.</p>
<p>Chairman Patrick Gillam said in a statement, &quot;The Asia Pacific region remains key to our future. There was a slight slowdown in Singapore and other economies during 1996 but indications are positive for 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>StanChart announced a 32 percent rise in pre-tax profits for 1996 to 870 million including exceptional items of 45 million stg, from 661 million in 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
